  "intro": {
    "en": "Today we leave the town behind and walk out onto the fields. On a spring morning, the open countryside is full of life: a bird that seems to climb a ladder of song in the sky, another tumbling over a ploughed field, a long-tailed gamebird that bursts out of the hedge.\n\nFarmland birds are among the ones that have declined most in Britain. That makes each one you find worth a bit more. We start with the black-and-white ones, then turn to the brown and the yellow.\n\nAt the end there's a quiz of eight questions, with birds from the last two lessons mixed in."
  },
